  "known_limitations": [
    "R1 (timestamp_grouped) can never reach coverage 1.0: the sampler truncates every timestamp group to a multiple of batch_size, so a fixed 21,904 of the 3,521,680 rows (0.622%) are never fed at any budget. The R1 coverage ceiling is 0.993784 and its plan therefore declares min_coverage 0.99; R2 keeps 1.0. This is the only guard change in either arm and it was fixed before any candidate score exists",
    "the 1.33 point exists only because the trajectory driver refuses fewer than two budget points; its checkpoint, predictions and metrics are excluded from every comparison, and all replays read modified_tlob_weights-screen10-1.32.json only",
    "metrics.json of the control replay has undefined cost/net-return sections because the plan evaluation block carries no single_side_rate; rank_ic and turnover are unaffected",
    "the R1 recipe also moves sampling to timestamp_grouped because config.py rejects a ranking loss without it, so R1 changes batch composition (and drops those 21,904 rows per epoch) as part of what the arm measures",
    "R2 triples the temporal head width (total_dim 320 -> 600, parameters 362k -> 1.20M), so its 1.32-point budget is the same sample count as the rung, not the same wall-clock cost"
  ],
